            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether copyright is a government program."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7908ff3073fe9be72d42d42f015739b01abb257c801b122bade49fca10ede5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7908ff3073-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg inquired whether a complimentary term like \u201cSlants Are Superior\u201d would fall outside the disparagement bar."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7908ff3073fe9be72d42d42f015739b01abb257c801b122bade49fca10ede5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7908ff3073-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked about the term \u201cscandalous.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7908ff3073fe9be72d42d42f015739b01abb257c801b122bade49fca10ede5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7908ff3073-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked whether the federal courts, as a government program, are open for actions to enforce infringement of a disparaging trademark."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7908ff3073fe9be72d42d42f015739b01abb257c801b122bade49fca10ede5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7908ff3073-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether the statute meets strict scrutiny or an intermediate level of review."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7908ff3073fe9be72d42d42f015739b01abb257c801b122bade49fca10ede5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7908ff3073-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked whether the statute is not clear enough for them to get it right."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7908ff3073fe9be72d42d42f015739b01abb257c801b122bade49fca10ede5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7908ff3073-0001-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor raised a hypothetical about a trademark that is also libelous and asked whether canceling it would abridge the First Amendment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7908ff3073fe9be72d42d42f015739b01abb257c801b122bade49fca10ede5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7908ff3073-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy likened trademark law to a public park, asking whether it is a public forum where any speech is allowed."
      }
    ],
