            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner (Malcolm L. Stewart), according to Petitioner (Malcolm L. Stewart), the petitioner argues that Section\u202f52(a)\u2019s disparagement provision merely places a reasonable limit on access to a government program and does not restrict speech, so it does not violate the First Amendment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "John C. Connell",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7908ff3073fe9be72d42d42f015739b01abb257c801b122bade49fca10ede5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7908ff3073-0001-0013"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to John C. Connell, the registration denial blocks the applicant from obtaining trademark protection, creating a burden that harms the ability to compete in the marketplace."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
